 "correction_note": "Op. 58, 'Six quartetti ... en deux livraisons, 1ere [2eme] parties' (Sieber, Paris). RISM has ONE record for all six quartets and zero incipits for any of them. Berlin's copy is scanned as two volumes under a MultivolumeWork anchor (PPN627503063) whose own IIIF manifest has an empty canvases list -- which reads as 'not scanned' unless you follow the METS to its children. Each livraison holds THREE quartets, not six: assigning the whole G 242-247 span to both was wrong, and made two different books look like duplicates. — '1re Partie'. Quartets I-III of Op. 58, in four part-books bound in sequence.",
 "corrected": true,
 "established_by": "Read off the scans, 2026-09-29. Title pages: livraison 1 is 'Op 58. 1re Partie', livraison 2 is 'Op 58. 2e Partie', both 'en deux Livraisons'. Quartet headings in the Violino I book of livraison 2 run IV. QUATUOR (p5), V. QUATUOR (p11), VI. QUATUOR (p17), then the Violino Secondo book restarts at IV (p23) -- so each livraison holds three quartets in four part-books, not six. Livraison 1 shows III. Quartetto at p14.",
 "livraison": 1,
